    "result_text": "All tests pass. `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract), and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `birthDate` \u2192 `ageBand` derivation for `POST /api/owners`. The request may now include an optional ISO `birthDate`; when present, the owner's response carries an `ageBand` of `MINOR` (under 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (65+), computed as completed years between `birthDate` and the owner's (business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate`. When no `birthDate` is supplied, `ageBand` is null/omitted.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (optional, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, and `ageBand` (readOnly enum `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` response schema. These regenerate the `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` and the `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persistent `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\", columnDefinition = \"DATE\")`) with getter/setter, so it survives the create \u2192 GET round-trip.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added a `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\n4. **`mapper/AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 standalone helper returning `AgeBandEnum` from the owner's birthDate vs registrationDate (null when no birthDate), matching the existing `ContactPreference`/`Locality` helper pattern.\n\n5. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired `ageBand` via `expression = \"java(AgeBand.of(owner))\"`, alongside the other derived fields.\n\n`birthDate` flows request \u2192 entity \u2192 response automatically via MapStruct's by-name mapping, and the JDBC repository maps it automatically through `BeanPropertyRowMapper`/`BeanPropertySqlParameterSource` \u2014 no manual persistence wiring needed. The endpoint's YAML pipeline was unchanged since this is a derived field on the existing build/respond flow.\n\nVerified: `./mvnw -o compile` clean, and `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
